<section id="problem-definition" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-7 sm:space-y-8">
  <div data-reveal class="ambient-scrim">
    <div class="hero-content-divider mb-2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <span class="act-marker">Section 1</span>
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight flex items-center gap-3 mt-1 section-heading-float">
      <span class="inline-block w-1 h-7 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#ff4d4d] to-[#ffb84d] rounded-sm" style="transform: skewX(-6deg);"></span>
      Problem Definition
    </h2>
    <p class="text-white/50 text-base sm:text-lg mt-2 section-heading-float">What it means for an action to continue naturally across a cinematic cut.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="glass-card rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-10 border border-white/[0.12] shadow-2xl space-y-6" data-reveal style="transition-delay:100ms">
    <p class="max-w-4xl text-[15px] sm:text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/90 font-light">
      <strong class="font-semibold text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-[#ff4d4d] to-[#ffb84d]">Action-Cut</strong>, also known as Match on Action, requires both action state and motion flow to continue naturally across a shot boundary. Given adjacent shots <em>S<sub>i</sub></em> and <em>S<sub>i+1</sub></em>, the tail of <em>S<sub>i</sub></em> should establish an action state and movement trajectory that are preserved and advanced by the head of <em>S<sub>i+1</sub></em>, maintaining directional continuity, timing, and momentum rather than resetting at the cut.
    </p>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-4" data-reveal style="transition-delay:180ms">
      <article class="method-component-card rounded-2xl border border-white/[0.10] bg-white/[0.04] p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all duration-300 chroma-hover">
        <span class="mb-3 inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-[#ff4d4d] to-[#ffb84d] text-sm font-bold text-[#20140f]">01</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white/90">Action state consistency</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/60">The outgoing frame and incoming frame preserve the same pose, contact, and stage of the action.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-component-card rounded-2xl border border-white/[0.10] bg-white/[0.04] p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all duration-300 chroma-hover">
        <span class="mb-3 inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-[#ff4d4d] to-[#ffb84d] text-sm font-bold text-[#20140f]">02</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white/90">Action flow continuity</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/60">Movement direction, timing, and momentum continue through the boundary without an abrupt reset or temporal flicker.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-component-card rounded-2xl border border-white/[0.10] bg-white/[0.04] p-4 sm:p-5 transition-all duration-300 chroma-hover">
        <span class="mb-3 inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-[#ff4d4d] to-[#ffb84d] text-sm font-bold text-[#20140f]">03</span>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white/90">Cinematic cut coherence</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/60">The edit remains narratively and physically plausible while the camera and shot language change.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
